architect › Plan sent to coder. What I decided and why:

**Root cause:** `slugify` filters on `/[^a-z0-9]+/` before any Unicode handling, so precomposed accented characters (`è`, `û`, `é`) are treated as punctuation and become dashes — hence `'Crème Brûlée'` → `'cr-me-br-l-e'`.

**Fix planned:** normalize to NFD first (splitting accented letters into base + combining mark), strip the combining marks `/[\u0300-\u036f]/g`, then keep the existing lowercase → dash-collapse → trim pipeline unchanged. This handles the base-letter reduction, dash collapsing, edge trimming, and punctuation-only → `''` all at once.

**Tests:** keep the existing one and add the reported case, accented caps, multi-dash runs, leading/trailing punctuation, empty string, and punctuation-only string.

**Check:** `bun test` must pass with 0 failures; coder will commit on `work/main` and report the output back. I'll consider the job done when that check passes.
